WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.868
-Look, I know you're all

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.202
just clapping for
the air conditioning,

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:04.503
but I'm still glad you're here.

00:00:04.503 --> 00:00:06.639
We're in the middle of
a giant heat wave right now

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.140
with temperatures in the 90s.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.141
It's crazy out here.

00:00:09.141 --> 00:00:10.410
I sat on a bench
for two minutes.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.145
When I got up,
my pants had grill marks.

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:13.546
-Really?!

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:16.715
-I saw that officials are
telling people that beer is

00:00:16.715 --> 00:00:18.318
not a good way to stay hydrated

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:20.186
and that you should drink water.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.654
When New Yorkers heard that,
they were like, "Okay.

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:22.921
Coors Light it is."

00:00:22.921 --> 00:00:26.426
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.530
Well, you guys, this heat wave
is really intense.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:32.999
This kind of weather
can be pretty rough,

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:35.167
so here now with some tips
on how to beat the heat

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:36.903
are The Roots.

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.071
-Thanks Jimmy.

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:41.541
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.209
-Tip number one --

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:46.445
stay out the sun
and drink lots of water.

00:00:46.445 --> 00:00:48.447
-It's a good one.
Here's what you do.

00:00:48.447 --> 00:00:51.350
You get yourself a Klondike bar

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:53.353
and use it like a bar of soap.

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:55.721
-Ah, interesting.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:58.424
-Take your pants off,
then remember you're at work

00:00:58.424 --> 00:01:01.460
and put them back on.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:02.562
-Close your eyes,

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:06.332
picture a penguin,
big, cute, slippery,

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:09.536
like an oversized toucan
wearing a tuxedo.

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:12.471
-Do what I do.

00:01:12.471 --> 00:01:14.307
Put your toupee in the freezer

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:17.143
so when you glue it on your head
in the morning,

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.946
it keeps your dome ice cold.

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:21.514
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:23.316
-Thank you.

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:25.985
Thank you for the tips.
I appreciate it.

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.587
Thank you very much, Roots.

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:30.589
I heard the heat could
cause another blackout

00:01:30.589 --> 00:01:32.591
here in New York.
[ Crowd murmuring ]

00:01:32.591 --> 00:01:34.727
So, think about that when
you're stepping into an elevator

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.028
with your annoying co-worker.

00:01:36.028 --> 00:01:39.131
Alright. It's like,
"Don't die on me now, power."

00:01:39.131 --> 00:01:41.134
"How was your summer?"
"Not good."

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:42.602
-[ Laughs ]
-That's right.

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:45.838
Officials think there will be
more blackouts at some point.

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:48.274
They know something bad's
coming, but they can't say when.

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.743
It's pretty much like
following Trump on Twitter.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:53.346
[ Laughter ]
Have you been following this?

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:55.014
Last night, the House
approved a resolution

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:57.217
to condemn
Trump's racist tweets.

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:58.584
It was the first time
it's happened

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:00.587
since William Howard Taft.

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:02.021
When he heard that,
Trump was like,

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:03.356
"Wow, what did he tweet?

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:05.992
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:07.894
Speaking of social media,
this is going viral.

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:09.929
Everybody's been using
this app called FaceApp.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:12.464
Have you guys heard of it?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:12.464 --> 00:02:13.933
It's creepy.
It's creepy.

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.435
It has a filter that
shows what you look like

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:16.535
when you're older.

00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:18.637
For example,
here's a photo of me,

00:02:18.637 --> 00:02:20.473
Here's me with the filter.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:21.974
Wow.

00:02:21.974 --> 00:02:23.843
[ Laughter ]
It's pretty crazy.

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:24.911
A lot of people are
giving it a try,

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:26.512
including some people
in Washington,

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:27.947
and the results are
kind of surprising.

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:29.081
Take a look.

00:02:29.081 --> 00:02:30.617
Here's the President's son
Eric Trump.

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:32.418
Here's him with the filter.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:35.388
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:41.460
Here's CNN host Anderson Cooper.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.896
Here's what he looks like
with the filter.

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:45.798
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:48.268
Up next is Treasury Secretary
Steve Mnuchin.

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:50.036
Here he is with the filter.

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:52.338
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:55.675
Here's Vladimir Putin.
Here's him with the old filter.

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:58.310
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:00.413
And finally, here's a photo
of Bernie Sanders,

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:02.315
and here he is as an old man.

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:04.650
[ Applause ]
-Looks pretty good.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:09.322
-Wow! Very realistic. Wow.
-Looks pretty good.

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:10.656
This is big.

00:03:10.656 --> 00:03:12.525
-Today, the Mexican
drug lord El Chapo

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.227
was sentenced to life in prison.

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:17.963
He has to turn over
$12.6 billion in drug money.

00:03:17.963 --> 00:03:19.865
Then Trump was like,
"See, I told you Mexico would

00:03:19.865 --> 00:03:21.200
pay for the wall.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:25.204
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:26.371
I told you."

00:03:26.371 --> 00:03:27.540
Listen to this.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.408
Taco Bell just came out
with a new burrito

00:03:29.408 --> 00:03:31.544
that's made with
the world's hottest pepper,

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:34.714
the Carolina Reaper.
-Ooh.

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:36.482
-It's for people who walk
into Taco Bell and think,

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.817
"How could I make this
bad decision even worse?"

00:03:38.817 --> 00:03:40.853
[ Laughter ]
Here's a crazy story.

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:43.388
The owners of a Miami restaurant
called Bacon Bitch

00:03:43.388 --> 00:03:45.358
is suing the owners...

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:48.428
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:50.763
-Too many jokes, yeah.
-It's not even...

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:51.898
[ Laughs ]

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:53.432
-The owners of
a Miami restaurant

00:03:53.432 --> 00:03:55.768
called Bacon Bitch --
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:57.069
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.069 --> 00:03:59.772
-Is it "Bacon Bitch"?
-Or is it "Bacon, Bitch"!

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:02.775
-Yeah.
-I don't know.

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:04.109
[ Applause ]

00:04:04.109 --> 00:04:06.345
-Where is the emphasis.
-Yeah. Okay. Alright.

00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:08.715
So, anyways, the owners of
the restaurant Bacon Bitch

00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:10.883
are suing the owners
of a San Diego restaurant

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.552
called Breakfast Bitch.

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:16.088
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:18.257
-"Breakfast, Bitch."
-[ Laughs ] Okay!

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:20.325
-Is that how that one is?

00:04:20.325 --> 00:04:22.328
-For stealing their idea.

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:24.964
Experts say it could be the
first case where a judge asks,

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:26.966
"How do you bitches plead?"

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.101
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:31.471
[ Applause ]

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:35.141
Bitch, please.

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:36.875
And finally,
I read about a man in Belgium

00:04:36.875 --> 00:04:38.211
who just set
the Guinness World Record

00:04:38.211 --> 00:04:41.247
for sitting on a toilet
for 116 straight hours.

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:42.248
[ Audience "oohs" ]

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:43.582
He wasn't trying
to break the record.

00:04:43.582 --> 00:04:45.752
He just ate Taco Bell's
new Carolina Reaper Burrito.

